    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93-a1">

                <pb facs="0230" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg174"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 864.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Direct United States Cable Company, Limited</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Palmerston Buildings, Old Broad
                                Street</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">London, E.
                            C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1876-01-27">27<hi
                                rendition="#italic">th January</hi>,
                    1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a letter from
                    my company to the President of the United States, praying that the United States
                    Government will grant such assistance to my company as will protect its cables
                    from future injury, and elucidate the facts connected with past
                    interruptions.</p>
                <p>I now beg leave to ask your excellency to kindly forward the letter and the
                    accompanying charts to the President.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, your excellency’s most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>G. <hi rendition="#small-caps">von</hi> CHANOIN,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Managing Director</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert C. Schenck</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary, Minister Plenipotentiary of the
                            United States of America</hi>, 5 <hi rendition="#italic">Westminster
                            Chambers, Victoria street, L. W.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
